<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Mišar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1806</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-serbian-uprising">First Serbian Uprising</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Mišar was fought in August 1806 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabac">Šabac</a> in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>, where Serbian rebels under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karadorde">Karađorđe</a> defeated a larger Ottoman army from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a>. Together with the victory at Deligrad, it secured the rebels' control of much of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgrade">Belgrade</a> region and is remembered as one of the great victories of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-serbian-uprising">First Serbian Uprising</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-misar.jpg" alt="Battle of Mišar" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Afanasij Scheloumoff · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Mi%C5%A1ar,_Afanasij_Scheloumoff.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
